      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of a triangle is always 180 degrees. Let's denote the measures of the three angles as \\(5x\\), \\(6x\\), and \\(7x\\), where \\(x\\) is a common multiplier. We can set up the following equation based on the sum of the angles:\n\n\\[5x + 6x + 7x = 180\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[18x = 180\\]\n\nTo find the value of \\(x\\), we divide both sides of the equation by 18:\n\n\\[x = \\frac{180}{18} = 10\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can find the measure of the smallest interior angle, which is \\(5x\\):\n\n\\[5x = 5 \\times 10 = 50\\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of the smallest interior angle is \\(\\boxed{50}\\) degrees.",
